+# keel compared with other spec-driven tools
+
+keel is not the only tool that puts a spec between you and an agent. This page
+says where it differs, and where something else is the better choice.
+
+"Not documented" means the tool's own page, checked on the date under
+[Sources](#sources), does not describe the property. It is not a claim that the
+tool cannot do it. Every keel cell links to the ADR or test that backs it.
+
+| | keel | spec-kit | Kiro | BMAD | Tessl | Elephant-Goldfish | Claude Code hooks |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| falsifiable criteria | Yes: each criterion carries an oracle ([test](../tests/oracle_sensitivity.rs)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| blocked as a verdict | Yes: pass, fail or blocked ([ADR-0002](../.keel/store/decisions/ADR-0002-blocked-is-a-verdict.md)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Partial: a hook can deny a tool call[^hooks] |
+| approvals bound to content | Yes: an approval binds to a hash ([ADR-0003](../.keel/store/decisions/ADR-0003-approvals-bind-to-a-hash.md)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| tamper-evident evidence | Yes: a hash-chained bundle verified offline ([test](../tests/bundle.rs)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| computed blast radius | Yes: recomputed, never trusted ([ADR-0009](../.keel/store/decisions/ADR-0009-blast-radius-is-recomputed.md)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| test-tampering review | Yes: added mocks and weakened assertions are flagged ([test](../tests/phase2.rs)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Partial: independent review sub-agents[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| lessons enforced as checks | Yes: enforced lessons become checks ([ADR-0007](../.keel/store/decisions/ADR-0007-enforced-lessons-are-not-injected.md)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Not documented[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+| agent drivers | Yes: a driver contract with a conformance suite ([test](../tests/driver.rs)) | Not documented[^speckit] | Not documented[^kiro] | Not documented[^bmad] | Not documented[^tessl] | Partial: plugin for several agents[^egm] | Not documented[^hooks] |
+
+## Where keel is weaker
+
+- **spec-kit**: choose it when you want a lightweight, template-driven
+  workflow with no gates to configure. keel asks for oracles, approvals and a
+  plan before an agent starts.
+- **Kiro**: choose it when you want the spec workflow inside an IDE, with no
+  command line. keel is a CLI.
+- **BMAD**: choose it when you want role-based agent personas that cover
+  product and architecture work as well as code. keel only judges the change.
+- **Tessl**: choose it when you want a managed registry of specs and library
+  usage guidance. keel keeps everything in your repository.
+- **Elephant-Goldfish**: choose it when you want a design document defended
+  before any code, reviewed by fresh sub-agents. keel checks the result, not
+  the reasoning behind it.
+- **Claude Code hooks**: choose them when you need one small, immediate rule,
+  such as blocking a command. A hook is a few lines; keel is a pipeline.
+
+## Sources
+
+[^speckit]: https://github.com/github/spec-kit (checked: 2026-11-04)
+[^kiro]: https://kiro.dev/docs/ (checked: 2026-11-04)
+[^bmad]: https://github.com/bmad-code-org/BMAD-METHOD (checked: 2026-11-04)
+[^tessl]: https://docs.tessl.io/ (checked: 2026-11-04)
+[^egm]: https://opensource.googleblog.com/2026/10/introducing-elephant-goldfish-model-plugin.html (checked: 2026-11-04)
+[^hooks]: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks (checked: 2026-11-04)
